{% comment %}
  Save-to-wishlist toggle.

  The wishlist is stored in the visitor's own browser (localStorage), not on an
  account and not in an app. That is a deliberate limit worth knowing: it does
  not follow someone to another device, and clearing site data clears it. In
  exchange it needs no login, no app subscription, and works on the first visit
  — which is when someone is most likely to save something.

  Only the product HANDLE is stored. Prices, availability and images are read
  live from /products/<handle>.js when the wishlist page renders, so a saved
  item can never show a stale price, and a deleted product drops out by itself.

  Usage:
    {% render 'wishlist-button', product: product %}                 icon only
    {% render 'wishlist-button', product: product, style: 'text' %}  icon + label

  Accepts: product (required), style ('icon' by default)
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign label = 'Save ' | append: product.title | append: ' to your wishlist'
  assign is_text = false
  if style == 'text'
    assign is_text = true
  endif
-%}
<button type="button"
        class="wish-btn{% if is_text %} wish-btn-text{% endif %}"
        data-wish-toggle="{{ product.handle }}"
        aria-pressed="false"
        aria-label="{{ label | escape }}">
  {%- comment -%} Two paths rather than a fill swap: the outline and the solid
      heart read differently at 20px, and a filled heart is the whole signal
      that something is saved. {%- endcomment -%}
  <svg class="wish-ico" width="{% if is_text %}19{% else %}20{% endif %}" height="{% if is_text %}19{% else %}20{% endif %}" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
    <path d="M20.8 5.6a5 5 0 0 0-7.1 0L12 7.3l-1.7-1.7a5 5 0 1 0-7.1 7.1L12 21.5l8.8-8.8a5 5 0 0 0 0-7.1z"></path>
  </svg>
  {%- if is_text -%}<span data-wish-label>Save for later</span>{%- endif -%}
</button>
